hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15570","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Hatim ibn Ismail al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, that a Jew had four dirhams upon him, and he sought help against him. He said: O Muhammad, I have four dirhams upon this one, and he has overcome me in them. He said: Give him his right. He said: By the One Who sent you with the truth, I cannot afford them. He said: Give him his right. He said: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I cannot afford them, I already told him that you will send us to Khaybar, and I hope you will enrich us with something, so I shall return and pay him. He said: Give him his right. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said three times, was not reviewed. So Ibn Abi Hadrad went out with him to the market, with a band upon his head, wrapped in a cloak. So he removed the turban from his head and wrapped himself with it, and removed the cloak and said: Buy from me this cloak. So he sold it to him for the four dirhams. An old woman passed and said: What is with you, O companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he told her. She said: Here, take this with a cloak upon it. She threw it upon him."
